# Mention-search provider. Auto-detected: twitterapi.io is preferred when
# configured (no 7-day lookback wall), falling back to the official X API.
#
# twitterapi.io - third-party X search reseller, no equivalent of the
# official API's 7-day recent-search wall, which is what actually blocks
# "who called it first" on a token that already ran. Priced per request/
# credit rather than a fixed monthly tier. Get a key at twitterapi.io.
TWITTERAPI_IO_KEY=

# Official X API v2 bearer token, used if TWITTERAPI_IO_KEY is unset.
#   Free  -> no search at all, use --mock
#   Basic -> recent search, 7-day lookback
#   Pro   -> full-archive search, pass --full-archive
# developer.x.com -> your App -> Keys and tokens -> Bearer Token
X_BEARER_TOKEN=

# Solana RPC. Defaults to https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com when unset.
# A free Helius key is worth it if the public endpoint rate-limits you -
# especially once this is deployed, since a hosted IP gets throttled harder
# than a local one.
# SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=YOUR_KEY
